sp.p:
Bless you, he won't accept it. I offer'd him money myself this morning;
                            but he damn'd my charity, said he was the child of Fortune, and it would
                            be an injustice to his mother not to depend upon her bounty.

At your service—I met with 'em a bargain; and determined to secure 'em
                            for your private reading. And to shew you my perfect disinterestedness,
                            you shall have 'em at half price.

Yes, but I tell you I will. I've had quite enough of your jolly nonsense;
                            I want a little, a little air, and a little quiet. Where is the
                            Gentleman —
